                                  information"; only the usage object, as the docs show it)
  anthropic_error.json            https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors ("Error shapes")
  openai_chat.json                https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create
                                  (the Default example's response)
  openai_responses_stream.sse     https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/responses/streaming-events
                                  (response.completed, compacted onto one data: line)
  openai_responses.json           the "response" object of that same event
  openai_responses_error.sse      same page, the "error" event

Composed from documented pieces (not a single verbatim example):

  anthropic_stream_error.sse      the basic example's message_start + the streaming page's
                                  "Error events" example (an error after HTTP 200)
  openai_chat_stream.sse          first chunk verbatim from the chat streaming-events page; the
                                  final usage chunk is built from the documented include_usage
                                  behaviour ("choices field will always be an empty array",
                                  usage null on other chunks); the docs show no verbatim one
  openai_error.json               the error envelope as openai-python reads it
                                  ({"error": {message, type, param, code}}); no verbatim example

Built from the schema only (https://ai.google.dev/api/generate-content: GenerateContentResponse,
UsageMetadata; the docs show requests, not responses):

  gemini_stream.sse               two alt=sse chunks, running totals in usageMetadata
